Menu="Utilities"
Title="Claude Code"
Icon="claude-code.png"
Desc="AI-powered coding assistant CLI"
---
<?php
$plugin_dir = "/boot/config/plugins/claude-code";
$cfg_file = "$plugin_dir/claude-code.cfg";

$cfg = file_exists($cfg_file) ? parse_ini_file($cfg_file) : [];
$appdata_path = $cfg['APPDATA_PATH'] ?? '';

// Fallback if config not yet populated (install script saves the auto-detected path)
if (empty($appdata_path)) {
    $appdata_path = '/mnt/user/appdata/claude-code';
}
$auth_dir = "$appdata_path/.claude";
$has_auth = is_dir($auth_dir);

// Check if array is started (check for actual mount, not just directory)
$array_started = trim(shell_exec("mountpoint -q /mnt/user 2>/dev/null && echo yes || echo no")) === "yes";

// Check if claude is installed
$claude_installed = trim(shell_exec("which claude 2>/dev/null")) !== "";
$claude_version = $claude_installed ? htmlspecialchars(trim(shell_exec("claude --version 2>/dev/null")) ?: "Unknown") : "";

// Check symlink status
$symlink_target = is_link("/root/.claude") ? readlink("/root/.claude") : null;
$symlink_ok = $symlink_target === "$appdata_path/.claude";
?>

<table class="tablesorter shift ups">
<thead><tr><th>_(Status)_</th></tr></thead>
</table>

<div style="width: 75%; float:left">

_(Claude Code)_:
: <?= $claude_installed
    ? "<span class='green-text'><b>$claude_version</b></span>"
    : "<span class='red-text'><b>_(Not installed)_</b></span>" ?>

_(Array)_:
: <?= $array_started
    ? "<span class='green-text'><b>_(Started)_</b></span>"
    : "<span class='red-text'><b>_(Not started)_</b></span>" ?>

_(Authentication)_:
: <?= $has_auth
    ? "<span class='green-text'><b>_(Configured)_</b></span>"
    : "<span class='orange-text'><b>_(Not authenticated)_</b></span>" ?>

_(Persistence Symlink)_:
: <?= $symlink_ok
    ? "<span class='green-text'><b>_(OK)_</b></span>"
    : "<span class='orange-text'><b>_(Not configured)_</b></span>" ?>

:claude_code_status_plug:
> Claude Code is an AI-powered coding assistant CLI from Anthropic.
>
> + **Claude Code**: Shows the installed version, or "Not installed" if the binary is not yet available.
> + **Array**: The Unraid array must be started for persistent storage to work.
> + **Authentication**: Shows whether Claude credentials have been saved. Run `claude` in the terminal to authenticate.
> + **Persistence Symlink**: Indicates whether `~/.claude` is correctly symlinked to your appdata folder.
:end

&nbsp;

<table class="tablesorter shift ups">
<thead><tr><th>_(Settings)_</th></tr></thead>
</table>

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="claude-code/claude-code.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-code/scripts/install-claude.sh">

_(Appdata Path)_:
: <input type="text" name="APPDATA_PATH" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($appdata_path);?>" placeholder="/mnt/user/appdata/claude-code" size="50">

:claude_code_appdata_path_plug:
> Path where Claude Code stores its configuration, authentication tokens, and cached binary.
> This should be on your array (not the flash drive) to avoid flash wear from the ~150MB binary.
>
> If left empty, the install script auto-detects the path from your Docker appdata configuration.
> Common locations:
>
> + `/mnt/user/appdata/claude-code` — Default (user share)
> + `/mnt/cache/appdata/claude-code` — Cache drive directly
:end

<input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

&nbsp;

<table class="tablesorter shift ups">
<thead><tr><th>_(Usage)_</th></tr></thead>
</table>

_(Getting Started)_:
: Open the Unraid terminal (top-right ` >_ ` icon) and run: `claude`

:claude_code_usage_plug:
> **First-Time Setup:**
>
> 1. Make sure the array is started.
> 2. Open terminal and run `claude`.
> 3. Follow the authentication prompts.
> 4. Your credentials are automatically saved to the appdata folder and persist across reboots.
>
> **Tips:**
>
> + Claude Code is re-installed automatically on each boot via the `disks_mounted` event hook.
> + The binary is cached in appdata so subsequent boots are fast (no re-download needed).
> + Check `/var/log/claude-code-install.log` if you encounter issues.
:end

&nbsp;

<table class="tablesorter shift ups">
<thead><tr><th>_(Maintenance)_</th></tr></thead>
</table>

_(Update Claude Code)_:
: <form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/bin/bash">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="-c">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[2]" value="source /boot/config/plugins/claude-code/claude-code.cfg 2>/dev/null; APPDATA_PATH=${APPDATA_PATH:-/mnt/user/appdata/claude-code}; rm -f &quot;$APPDATA_PATH/bin/claude&quot; /root/.local/bin/claude /usr/local/bin/claude; /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-code/scripts/install-claude.sh">
<input type="submit" value="_(Update)_">
</form>

:claude_code_update_plug:
> Clears the cached Claude Code binary and re-downloads the latest version from Anthropic.
> Use this after a new Claude Code release to get the latest features and fixes.
:end

_(Reinstall Claude Code)_:
: <form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-code/scripts/install-claude.sh">
<input type="submit" value="_(Reinstall)_">
</form>

:claude_code_reinstall_plug:
> Re-runs the install script without clearing the cached binary.
> If the cached binary is still valid, this is a fast operation.
> Use this if Claude Code stopped working but you don't need the latest version.
:end
